(4987771, 723573, 71657, '<td valign="top">Guess you wasted a ten thinking this was Irene''s shot.  Before long, so many people will be doing water shots, no one will know who''s is who''s and level the playing field.  What a rip.<br/> <br/><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by DrAchoo:</b></div><hr/><i> Hi Irene. </i></td></tr></table></td>', 'Guess you wasted a ten thinking this was Irene''s shot.  Before long, so many people will be doing water shots, no one will know who''s is who''s and level the playing field.  What a rip. Originally posted by DrAchoo: Hi Irene. ', '2008-10-02 18:05:59.000000', NULL, 0),
(4987880, 724415, 98141, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by Shaka:</b></div><hr/><i> Haha!  Sandi, I remember seeing this picture in the "Bummer" Challenge.  :)  I really liked it!  (How did you get your background to be completely black?)<br/> <br/>~Kristi </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>This is my pumpkin in the parking lot of my workplace after dark, the lighting is all done by my truck''s headlights (I agree with the comments that don''t like the lighting, it''s something I need to work on in general) and the Kmart smokers next door thought I was crazy for smashing a pumpkin in the middle of a vacant parking lot at 9:30 at night. So, long story short, I guess the answer to your question is that it was night. :)</td>', 'Originally posted by Shaka: Haha!  Sandi, I remember seeing this picture in the "Bummer" Challenge.  :)  I really liked it!  (How did you get your background to be completely black?) ~Kristi   This is my pumpkin in the parking lot of my workplace after dark, the lighting is all done by my truck''s headlights (I agree with the comments that don''t like the lighting, it''s something I need to work on in general) and the Kmart smokers next door thought I was crazy for smashing a pumpkin in the middle of a vacant parking lot at 9:30 at night. So, long story short, I guess the answer to your question is that it was night. :)', '2008-10-02 18:54:23.000000', NULL, 0),
